  journalLore: The bog keeps what falls into it. This one fell in long ago, horse and rider, and came up again grown through with the same green rot as the wild horses of the mire. It rides out when the mist is thick.
  journalAdvice: 'Holy light and fire both hurt it. Its blade poisons, so carry an antidote, and don''t stand in the fog it leaves. It charges from far off: sidestep and strike as it turns. It frightens horses.'
  journalHabitat: The old barrows and the ground around them
